🔐 Hands-on 3 — envFrom 🔐

- This time, instead of selecting individual Secret keys, we'll inject all keys from the Secret into the Pod as environment variables.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 01 - Creation of Secrets

apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret

metadata:
  name: db-secret

# default secret type
type: Opaque

data:
  username: cGF5bWVudF91c2Vy
  password: cGF5bWVudEAxMjM=
  dbname: cGF5bWVudF9kYg==

# kubectl apply -f db-secret.yaml

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 02 - Create the Pod

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: app-secret-pod-03
spec:
  containers:
    - name: app-container
      image: busybox:1.36
      command:
        - sh
        - -c
        - |
          echo "DB_USERNAME = $DB_USERNAME"
          echo "DB_NAME = $DB_NAME"
          sleep 3600
      envFrom:
        - secretRef:
            name: db-secret

# kubectl apply -f secret-pod.yaml


The important part:-
  envFrom:
    - secretRef:
        name: app-secret

This means, "Take all key-value pairs from db-secret and make them environment variables inside the container."

